What this fork changes
----------------------

- The product identity: product name, window title, icons and theme; the bundle
  identifier (com.medagent.workbench, renamed in 0.8.0 from com.ai4s.workbench)
  and the app's own version line and release feed. It is a distinct application
  to the OS, not an upstream build.
- The bundled domain content: the science connectors, the skill set, the
  one-click workflow prompts and the example project are medical instead of
  general-science. The medical skills added here live in
  runtime/skills/core/{clinical-evidence,medical-stats,med-figures,case-report,
  literature-review,citation-reviewer,paper-to-report} and the example in
  examples/clinical-diagnostics.
- Dependency and repository hygiene: an unreferenced `xlsx` tarball dependency was
  removed, and `.gitattributes` pins text files to LF.

Everything else — the agent runtime integration, the desktop shell, the terminal,
the provenance ledger, the gateway, the browser and computer-use layers — is
upstream work, unmodified except where a commit says otherwise.

